A||||2||Tigger||Lost a starter bolt...||||9||
Z||000000||Tigger||10-08-2000||10:48 PM||||I lost a starter bolt Friday morning on my way to work but didn't find out till I got home.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Went to leave work and my starter made an aweful noise but the engine started.  Got home and figured the recent rain must have caused some corrosion in one of the bearings in the starter motor or something because I had no problems that morning.  Got home, engine way to hot to touch.  So, while she cooled down I ran out and bought a new starter.  <P>Got home, jacked her up, crawled under, and to my suprise I had only one starter bolt!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">  The other one was loose!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">  Geeze, talk about luck, I was planning on going on the Michigan Fiero Club Color Tour this weekend, I would have been majorly screwed if I had gone that morning.  I bailed out on not going just a week before.  Fortunatly I only started the car once and didn't chuck any teeth or cause any major grindage on the flywheel.  Got a new bolt and used some thread lock on the bolts and bolted the new starter in.<P>Anyway, just to let you all know to check those pesky bolts next time yer under your Fieros.  BTW, Has anyone had this happen to them?  <P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tigger.gif">          <BR> <A HREF="mailto:RacingStripes@hotmail.com">RacingStripes@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||9
Z||000001||theogre||10-10-2000||09:31 AM||||that's not all that uncommon. it can happen to any starter, not just GM. When this happpens to GM starters you want to replace the remaining bolt if it got even a little bent. bending weakens them. With the much beating these 2 bolts get you want to avoid any thing that might break.<P>GM starter bolts usually have a knerled area on them. It's suposed to prevent them comming out. I still use locktight on them. (Make sure its the removable stuff!)||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tigger||10-10-2000||08:33 PM||||I checked the other bolt to see and it didn't get bent because it hadn't work its way out like the shorter one plus I think I caught the problem before driving with it like it was for long.  <P>Yep, I used the blue serviceable locktight.<P>By the way I appreciate all the work you've done in putting together your cave.  <P>"Good work my Friend"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Thank You!||||reg||14
